values ('e8b4d2a7-1c59-4f06-9a31-5d0e7c3b6f18', 'social-and-behavioral-determinants-of-health', 'Social and Behavioral Determinants of Health', 'This course examines how social structures, policies, institutions, environments, relationships, stress processes, and behavior shape population health and inequity. Students learn to measure determinants, reason about causal pathways, interpret disparities without stigmatizing groups, engage communities, and design multilevel interventions. The course integrates social epidemiology, behavioral science, policy, equity, and public communication.');

