  'Social and Behavioral Determinants of Health',
  'This course examines how social structures, policies, institutions, environments, relationships, stress processes, and behavior shape population health and inequity. Students learn to measure determinants, reason about causal pathways, interpret disparities without stigmatizing groups, engage communities, and design multilevel interventions. The course integrates social epidemiology, behavioral science, policy, equity, and public communication.',
  $sbdhjson${"slug": "social-and-behavioral-determinants-of-health", "title": "Social and Behavioral Determinants of Health", "description": "This course examines how social structures, policies, institutions, environments, relationships, stress processes, and behavior shape population health and inequity. Students learn to measure determinants, reason about causal pathways, interpret disparities without stigmatizing groups, engage communities, and design multilevel interventions. The course integrates social epidemiology, behavioral science, policy, equity, and public communication.", "topics": [{"id": "4a533441-e63b-4b7e-bb35-19eb76587b30", "type": "topic", "title": "Determinants Frameworks, Health Equity, and Causal Thinking", "description": "Establish how social conditions, power, institutions, environments, biology, and behavior interact to produce patterned health outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "fbcbf65e-3a5a-472e-8077-6a72dc536434", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core frameworks", "description": "Students compare SDOH, social production, fundamental cause, ecosocial, and political-economy perspectives.", "children": [{"id": "e6d1e14c-8c98-4b5f-a981-02acb8af5c2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Upstream, midstream, and downstream determinants"}, {"id": "6b7737c4-58fb-4231-a88e-c7e222290904", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural, intermediary, and individual pathways"}, {"id": "823b520c-20db-4ba3-b8d4-eb4ccde90e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Health difference, disparity, inequity, and equity"}]}, {"id": "2f6274df-43ce-4040-b7d3-0ceb42da861b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causal pathways", "description": "The point is mechanisms rather than determinant lists.", "children": [{"id": "5a5986da-ca43-49d8-9cb3-cb999a179290", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, psychosocial, behavioral, environmental, and healthcare pathways"}, {"id": "17093e3f-e0a7-4017-b498-fc47ae91d48e", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediation, moderation, feedback, and cumulative exposure"}, {"id": "5b496f4b-ee13-4e09-8ebc-e9a879c83f16", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection, reverse causation, and confounding"}]}, {"id": "bf781cf8-bfab-4dbf-81b8-2e0cdc0fcdd2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and action", "description": "Students connect explanation to public responsibility.", "children": [{"id": "826812fa-4e86-47d0-8d6c-c6fa8b7f8bd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Human rights and social justice"}, {"id": "9c547bc1-adc5-403e-a72d-dff813d4854f", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal, targeted, and proportionate universal approaches"}, {"id": "47cb603f-e599-4b18-85a5-61b450fb245f", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding blame, stigma, and deficit framing"}]}]}, {"id": "7786f4dd-584d-40c3-b539-766965982e9f", "type": "topic", "title": "Measuring Social Conditions and Health Inequities", "description": "Use valid, transparent measures while recognizing that categories and datasets are socially produced.", "children": [{"id": "f82a8afb-1e3d-4dea-b032-87439368c42d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Variables and indicators", "description": "Students operationalize complex constructs.", "children": [{"id": "3c31bf33-5d04-4e80-9b43-0277bac5377d", "type": "concept", "title": "Income, wealth, education, occupation, deprivation, and hardship"}, {"id": "ac56e4fa-6af8-4f56-bea7-57a042dd8000", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual, household, neighborhood, institutional, and policy measures"}, {"id": "aca9deb5-a4f8-46e5-82e1-00e4217fd381", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute/relative and objective/subjective measures"}]}, {"id": "d89fb25b-6234-41b6-ad04-a36e216d2d81", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inequality measurement", "description": "The goal is clear comparison across groups, places, and time.", "children": [{"id": "217ea71b-45ad-45b0-b18a-5a6ca20658aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Rates, ratios, differences, concentration, gradients, and population impact"}, {"id": "5591f667-b146-4646-9c28-a0907c4cfdf2", "type": "concept", "title": "Age standardization and denominator choice concepts"}, {"id": "a538068c-8967-41b8-a9d4-f2a4fe54e676", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectional and small-area reporting"}]}, {"id": "35f861a2-5793-4c33-b00d-1bebde52bd64", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data quality and ethics", "description": "Students examine missingness, misclassification, privacy, and harm.", "children": [{"id": "9878eb34-837f-4695-a0f5-2d75ad913b54", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-identification and administrative categories"}, {"id": "4ad466bb-1193-4046-a92d-2eaf4a13101f", "type": "concept", "title": "Data disaggregation and unstable estimates"}, {"id": "c765be10-c087-4442-b63b-d3e8c0a18882", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance, consent, sovereignty, and deficit narratives"}]}]}, {"id": "8c5e42e9-a053-4a25-a5db-c648bfd47141", "type": "topic", "title": "Socioeconomic Position, Income, Wealth, and Poverty", "description": "Explain how command over resources, security, status, and opportunity shapes exposure and health across a gradient.", "children": [{"id": "1efebd6e-289c-4f2b-a753-f0f0c831ac1b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dimensions of socioeconomic position", "description": "Students distinguish income, wealth, education, occupation, and class.", "children": [{"id": "1b1e2695-fdf8-4b70-ab47-71b8cf3adc34", "type": "concept", "title": "Current resources versus accumulated assets/debt"}, {"id": "b5a11af0-df9c-4838-b117-8270f84dbd18", "type": "concept", "title": "Employment status, occupational prestige, and working conditions"}, {"id": "e4847266-693f-4ac3-b092-ce1ed47464b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Subjective social status and relative deprivation"}]}, {"id": "cf3b0ee2-a0bd-455d-bc07-8f872a12af9f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health pathways", "description": "The point is why gradients persist beyond extreme poverty.", "children": [{"id": "88522954-2094-49d2-a8a0-5ae80bb3ce7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Material conditions and access to essentials"}, {"id": "19dbf4e3-e6c9-4d8e-b2bd-bbe9baeed9fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Stress, control, status, and social participation"}, {"id": "1b93fb94-26e1-4b34-88dc-cf8e78484af0", "type": "concept", "title": "Health behavior opportunities and healthcare access"}]}, {"id": "62dcf18a-ef02-4f4d-9f39-c47ea2fdd3ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy responses", "description": "Students compare income and service interventions.", "children": [{"id": "c3371784-c7ee-4d7a-88b9-42d2dfc7bda7", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimum wage, tax credits, cash transfers, and social insurance"}, {"id": "a0824f32-c8b6-4982-aa45-c7ea655e4e37", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt, benefits cliffs, and administrative burden"}, {"id": "97f94aed-7dcc-4ac7-be48-b2b8134f967f", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal services and anti-poverty policy"}]}]}, {"id": "d3c23a58-ca6e-4381-b32a-79e7050ce502", "type": "topic", "title": "Structural Racism, Ethnicity, Migration, and Discrimination", "description": "Analyze racialized health inequities as products of historical and contemporary systems rather than biological race.", "children": [{"id": "c1b5f37e-a04a-49a3-98db-5a2e43e8e8b0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural pathways", "description": "Students trace policy and institutional mechanisms.", "children": [{"id": "a56849fb-26a4-4554-8084-db078a1b3f91", "type": "concept", "title": "Segregation, housing, education, labor, criminal legal, and environmental policy"}, {"id": "4b13fbc9-3cc1-4335-aea9-0d917fa3ea4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Wealth extraction and unequal investment"}, {"id": "304448fd-8472-48f2-aca2-90c6a0c04044", "type": "concept", "title": "Healthcare access, quality, and algorithmic bias"}]}, {"id": "263e0c01-6a68-499b-b7ff-8219e21f46ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Discrimination and embodiment", "description": "The goal is connecting interpersonal/institutional exposure to health.", "children": [{"id": "1e08b699-190d-403a-8aa6-78cb35528695", "type": "concept", "title": "Acute/chronic discrimination and vigilance"}, {"id": "39d9d8c5-4bdd-4608-816d-1ea7ff944c5d", "type": "concept", "title": "Stress physiology, mental health, and care avoidance"}, {"id": "f0098d62-c1d7-41af-ad24-aec79c075c60", "type": "concept", "title": "Colorism, xenophobia, and language discrimination"}]}, {"id": "4b811cf8-81b3-44f5-99ec-c57a78275713", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Migration and ethnicity", "description": "Students avoid treating diverse populations as homogeneous.", "children": [{"id": "b7c9d611-a1dc-4e93-9030-218ad1358e26", "type": "concept", "title": "Nativity, legal status, displacement, and acculturation contexts"}, {"id": "b9e78010-9c40-42e5-8004-5ec83a09ed2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Healthy-immigrant selection and erosion concepts"}, {"id": "f75384fc-a34f-4fb6-b673-e82a815ecae7", "type": "concept", "title": "Data categories, within-group variation, and community strengths"}]}]}, {"id": "793ceab7-a6cb-4f31-adb1-66e0539ce087", "type": "topic", "title": "Gender, Sexuality, and Health", "description": "Examine how gender systems, sexual orientation, reproductive governance, roles, violence, and care work influence health.", "children": [{"id": "2a6b2734-6191-4196-ae55-4b73fb8aa600", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gender as social structure", "description": "Students distinguish sex-related biology from gendered exposure and power.", "children": [{"id": "0309d069-af54-4cee-8779-22dacf65219d", "type": "concept", "title": "Norms, roles, occupations, income, and unpaid care"}, {"id": "f8f9a3a7-c19d-413a-8b66-dc68fc048bb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Masculinities, femininities, and gender diversity"}, {"id": "126fad07-81e4-4df6-9b34-d52ac33dc928", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional policy and discrimination"}]}, {"id": "a5e9d742-57bc-440c-9cd6-a94510bf408c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sexual and gender minority health", "description": "The point is minority stress and structural access, not identity as risk.", "children": [{"id": "f90ebf30-e65e-4b58-8a6f-5c756fabc413", "type"