lay, undertreatment, pain, maternal care, and referral patterns"}, {"id": "43cc2f7e-ad2c-4f68-a313-8a2932ecc6b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Implicit/explicit bias and structural workflows"}, {"id": "dcfc5f6f-f842-43ec-b9d2-c3a525da7778", "type": "concept", "title": "Patient experience and safety"}]}, {"id": "7117a380-4b2b-4466-ac82-3a44f4bb24ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "System responses", "description": "Students compare strategies and limits.", "children": [{"id": "6d9ac232-c859-45a0-b073-eaf60eacd0a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Community health centers and safety net"}, {"id": "722d222c-7bd3-43ff-8af6-98f0c4aad3dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Workforce diversity, interpreters, navigation, and community health workers"}, {"id": "3b020e9b-5a3b-4c1c-8528-a7734540548f", "type": "concept", "title": "Payment, accountability, and equity measurement"}]}]}, {"id": "f771701a-d967-4ab2-b0ec-f0dea4680df4", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Relationships, Networks, and Community Context", "description": "Explain how connection, isolation, social support, norms, cohesion, and collective efficacy influence health.", "children": [{"id": "04895a67-bfac-44b0-ad06-b4815a35182c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social ties and support", "description": "Students distinguish network structure from supportive function.", "children": [{"id": "40f665a8-a19b-4fcf-aeed-f0cbe5c81a69", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotional, informational, instrumental, and appraisal support"}, {"id": "d393bacc-e881-465f-a373-f4d2620bcbc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Network size, density, diversity, and reciprocity"}, {"id": "e261039e-45d7-46ac-a3f7-0d3cd9c33474", "type": "concept", "title": "Isolation, loneliness, caregiving, and bereavement"}]}, {"id": "31272463-1ceb-4295-aa41-4afc278015ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Norms and diffusion", "description": "The goal is understanding how behaviors and information spread.", "children": [{"id": "63a7204f-26a9-4fb7-b095-946af98167e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer influence and social learning"}, {"id": "97c4bdb9-7eca-4106-bbcb-20a109e778d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Contagion, clustering, and homophily concepts"}, {"id": "2e58e38c-678e-4e79-8a8b-eaeb55bcb9b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Trusted messengers and network interventions"}]}, {"id": "064310cd-f028-49c7-91aa-49cadcb945f9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community capacity", "description": "Students identify strengths and collective action.", "children": [{"id": "747ff32b-caa4-4347-8b83-5f8d6f5cc67a", "type": "concept", "title": "Social capital and collective efficacy"}, {"id": "ae54a0e7-cf80-444a-8313-5cda3f33299a", "type": "concept", "title": "Mutual aid, faith/cultural institutions, and civic participation"}, {"id": "7787e53e-36c9-4093-97ab-92baa7c87f3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Community violence, trust, and healing"}]}]}, {"id": "0b9190e9-4993-4ad6-bab4-7f23d0229754", "type": "topic", "title": "Stress, Allostatic Load, and Psychosocial Pathways", "description": "Connect chronic social exposure to neuroendocrine, immune, cardiovascular, metabolic, and behavioral processes without biological determinism.", "children": [{"id": "266ec522-77c6-42e6-ac55-6b5b53c0e685", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stress process", "description": "Students distinguish stressors, appraisal, resources, and responses.", "children": [{"id": "790fe4a3-d473-4393-83c6-8cc5ea7fc1a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Acute, chronic, daily, traumatic, and anticipatory stress"}, {"id": "83fd7c4c-bd2d-476e-b985-33e50fa1f66a", "type": "concept", "title": "Control, predictability, threat, and social evaluation"}, {"id": "45f0ba09-4cce-4363-b28e-fe7bd92c02be", "type": "concept", "title": "Coping, support, and resilience"}]}, {"id": "fa1b30d2-3d5a-45f4-9fcb-16e7a8f4bb26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Embodiment", "description": "The point is repeated adaptation and physiologic cost.", "children": [{"id": "ca64d455-0fbe-405d-8248-574a5e92647f", "type": "concept", "title": "HPA/autonomic and inflammatory pathways"}, {"id": "7fbdce00-f602-4d81-add6-7223ae62f234", "type": "concept", "title": "Allostasis and allostatic-load concepts"}, {"id": "da907299-0bff-4238-b9ab-047b42cceb93", "type": "concept", "title": "Sleep, mental health, substance use, and cardiometabolic effects"}]}, {"id": "e4162df0-5043-486f-bbd9-343b53f8d27e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intervention implications", "description": "Students compare individual support with structural prevention.", "children": [{"id": "18309bce-d0a2-41a2-bfb5-306a61de3f24", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed and healing-centered systems"}, {"id": "35de4d7f-2ae9-4d0f-ba3b-5ee25443228c", "type": "concept", "title": "Work, housing, income, discrimination, and violence interventions"}, {"id": "e392708d-598d-451f-9ada-8b7d7d39d06f", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding resilience rhetoric that excuses harmful conditions"}]}]}, {"id": "9c74f93e-6e33-44eb-9e8c-389b7fb6735a", "type": "topic", "title": "Behavioral Science and Health Behavior Theories", "description": "Use behavioral theories to explain action while embedding behavior in social and environmental opportunity.", "children": [{"id": "141e8704-eb80-47b3-906f-890688b867ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Individual-level theories", "description": "Students compare constructs and appropriate uses.", "children": [{"id": "b168841d-3634-46de-a22f-968d74e13856", "type": "concept", "title": "Health Belief Model, Theory of Planned Behavior, and self-efficacy"}, {"id": "10d0bfda-7ff7-4553-90c8-6583a1388432", "type": "concept", "title": "Stages/processes of change concepts"}, {"id": "42ae8ec4-80a2-4a0a-a61c-576924e185a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk perception, intention, skills, and habits"}]}, {"id": "59072a1b-b0f7-45a8-85fb-2302b28f8e26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interpersonal/social theories", "description": "The goal is understanding relationships, norms, and learning.", "children": [{"id": "57987808-4147-4ef3-8b9e-a412b8a125c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Social Cognitive Theory"}, {"id": "3f773aff-ab4f-48ce-8335-3def3b5ca2ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Social support and network influence"}, {"id": "17512746-ef0a-47ee-bfa0-40c642b5e7ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Diffusion of innovations"}]}, {"id": "00d1af36-752d-410b-bb1f-99f648f3257a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavioral economics and ethics", "description": "Students examine defaults, friction, scarcity, and choice architecture.", "children": [{"id": "88407895-dfb8-44ed-b92f-b186c7afa1c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Present bias, limited attention, and hassle factors"}, {"id": "8925058c-70fe-419c-980c-53c71ceadce6", "type": "concept", "title": "Nudges, boosts, and sludge reduction"}, {"id": "02362dd4-c3b0-4c88-bb89-8a1785afd734", "type": "concept", "title": "Autonomy, transparency, manipulation, and equity"}]}]}, {"id": "39d3967d-68b3-4537-9687-91cbb6cd2827", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Ecological and Systems Approaches", "description": "Design explanations and interventions across individual, interpersonal, organizational, community, and policy levels.", "children": [{"id": "aa6480cc-9897-48d0-a0d3-c758a68a88b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multilevel analysis", "description": "Students locate determinants and actors at interacting levels.", "children": [{"id": "0b5cb908-7f8c-4cbc-a6ae-1aa2aec8e749", "type": "concept", "title": "Nested contexts and cross-level effects"}, {"id": "60ac9ba2-f85d-4747-82c1-d48cc3c0564f", "type": "concept", "title": "Settings and institutional routines"}, {"id": "847dcd4c-d1ba-4325-a5f8-5307a6af32c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback, delays, and unintended consequences"}]}, {"id": "be6ddf06-8056-4715-8b95-4c86846d0475", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Systems tools", "description": "The point is making complexity discussable.", "children": [{"id": "be2e386e-f068-46ad-b5c6-dffd91730e71", "type": "concept", "title": "Causal-loop diagrams and systems maps"}, {"id": "1ce04336-09d9-4d44-9dd6-9c6e78b424cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Leverage points and policy resistance"}, {"id": "e82fb97e-9b28-4cc7-a232-575f3673b7fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario and stakeholder analysis"}]}, {"id": "55b6f772-98a3-4afe-a1ad-fb1080d5b2bc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multilevel intervention", "description": "Students build coherent packages rather than disconnected activities.", "children": [{"id": "31a7773b-2bfd-4d3f-b5cd-002741b29984", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual support plus environmental/policy change"}, {"id": "cc5da3a1-8b44-48aa-8daf-faebb15912ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation roles and coordination"}, {"id": "ef3e5898-512a-4a5f-a61a-6c13ed8c2631", "type": "concept", "title": "Synergy, conflict, and evaluation across levels"}]}]}, {"id": "8ec988eb-6045-4bcf-9fe4-f8f36e5675a4", "type": "topic", "title": "Community-Engaged and Participatory Public Health", "description": "Work with communities as co-producers of knowledge, priorities, interventions, and accountability.", "children": [{"id": "eae9a7b2-895e-4736-ab27-c967349dfc92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Engagement principles", "description": "Students distinguish outreach, consultation, involvement, collaboration, and shared governance.", "children": [{"id": "ad7e0196-0906-4295-9200-90953d965975", "type": "concept", "title": "Trust, reciprocity, transparency, and long-term relationship"}, {"id": "5913f83a-6d8f-4b45-93d9-d8279373a729", "type": "concept", "title": "Community expertise and decision power"}, {"id": "cff63f37-2039-4ce4-bbdc-578ce11893f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Compensation, language, accessibility, and scheduling"}]}, {"id": "3dee1630-6479-4289-a3e4-8b15c7994fae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Participatory methods", "description": "The goal is useful evidence and shared interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "2c3159a2-acea-4863-ab19-8bc3b456555f", "type": "concept", "title": "CBPR principles, advisory boards, focus groups, PhotoVoice, and community mapping"}, {"id": "b26ae7d6-e19e-450f-a612-b2188b687731", "type": "concept", "title": "Data ownership and dissemination"}, {"id": "1936372d-9798-4293-aa3f-d295186b1786", "type": "concept", "title": "Power-sharing and conflict"}]}, {"id": "f086627d-24e7-45a6-aa74-2b41748648e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Action and sustainability", "description": "Students connect findings to community priorities and resources.", "children": [{"id": "401e5747-58da-4673-95e7-81693dfcfa05", "type": "concept", "title": "Co-design and implementation"}, {"id": "1aed3b93-c8da-434b-bc63-f0fe471eb778", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity strengthening and leadership"}, {"id": "a4f6cec5-9c0d-4719-ae18-25b21ac573fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Return of results and accountable exit"}]}]}, {"id": "e95213f2-1a95-4870-b99d-21859de5a0ab", "type": "topic", "title": "Policy, Structural Interventions, and Health in All Policies", "description": "Analyze how laws, budgets, institutional rules, and political power distribute health opportunities.", "children": [{"id": "4637d854-7344-4517-b3f9-feadb7936d8d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy pathways", "description": "Students trace design to exposure, behavior, resources, and outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "fdc1f73c-2cca-4c16-9ba5-8416e0297248", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility, benefits, taxes, regulation, enforcement, and administration"}, {"id": "3637a440-715b-4b88-9d0f-ef1462007887", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative burden and take-up"}, {"id": "5d850f96-6c08-4a92-a263-cb33276f58f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy feedback and path dependence"}]}, {"id": "c10f3951-b093-4c54-8c11-b180c8b8e0d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural intervention domains", "description": "The point is changing conditions rather than only counseling people.", "children": [{"id": "ed894d8e-6c1d-4bff-8935-22be0989e3ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Income, housing, education, labor, transport, food, environment, and healthcare"}, {"id": "947a2476-0e41-4df3-b8cb-457f7d44c4dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal versus targeted design"}, {"id": "4a00b5e2-77ba-4049-940b-156898298bcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Distribution, unintended effects, and political durability"}]}, {"id": "7fc3a38a-738a-4b8c-b236-c59c7a3f6e79", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health in All Policies", "description": "Students integrate health/equity into decisions outside health agencies.", "children": [{"id": "328e3739-717d-4eb4-bfc8-e4a713cab350", "type": "concept", "title": "Health/equity impact assessment"}, {"id": "0f74ccda-2c2f-4022-b95c-789392b5db31", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectoral governance and accountability"}, {"id": "b3090325-6a40-414c-8650-f82e12c2ea4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Budgeting, monitoring, and community participation"}]}]}, {"id": "49e584a6-9f07-4d33-9b8f-da955bfcc6d3", "type": "topic", "title": "Intervention Design, Evaluation, and Equity Communication", "description": "Translate determinants into multilevel action and assess whether implementation and outcomes reduce inequity.", "children": [{"id": "3d8e2a30-565f-4e73-9e85-065f112e841f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design", "description": "Students align problem, mechanism, population, setting, and intervention.", "children": [{"id": "cea8cff0-66cd-4eef-9fb8-d4bec7c06f5d", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory of change and logic model"}, {"id": "931f0947-e204-4352-b38e-242e0122395c", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence, adaptation, feasibility, and implementation"}, {"id": "4c499afd-910f-4c27-8148-376c619c2e53", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal, targeted, and proportionate strategies"}]}, {"id": "f01afb70-2cee-4580-b39c-3a310d67a502", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation", "description": "The goal is learning what works, for whom, where, why, and at what cost.", "children": [{"id": "c56c5bf1-d807-4cfb-94c7-b0d47e4f5c27", "type": "concept", "title": "Process, outcome, impact, and economic evaluation"}, {"id": "92ed219c-d5bc-4b77-bbae-318d9374e5f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Reach, dose, fidelity, adaptation, and context"}, {"id": "9cb7c0c1-3f20-49c0-a940-baecba83a678", "type": "concept", "title": "Effect heterogeneity, equity indicators, and unintended effects"}]}, {"id": "da4c43ee-847c-4624-9acf-2a416a62c648", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Communication", "description": "Students present determinants without stigma or fatalism.", "children": [{"id": "3db1cd5d-2ee5-40c1-8b05-86cc81b7fc77", "type": "concept", "title": "Data visualization and uncertainty"}, {"id": "667c30a4-edd8-48d1-93ff-8bc4ea12d506", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain-language policy brief and community presentation"}, {"id": "67b8a4d1-1646-4acb-bb0e-65da7f7fd666", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths-based framing, causal humility, and actionable recommendations"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$sbdhjson$::jsonb,
